WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.120
It’s gone!

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.580
Gone, gone, g-gone...

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.110
The cake I was saving is gone!

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.130
My snacks are gone too, meow.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.370
Did that <i>thing</i>
hork our stuff down again...?!

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.760
Well, I hid mine somewhere
<i>completely</i> safe.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.090
Huh?

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.720
N-No way...!

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.570
B-By all means,
go ahead and keep eating...

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.280
If you like it,
we’re happy, meow.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.580
We can buy more
if you need more...

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.290
It’s been eating even more
than usual lately, meow...

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.250
<i>All</i> the money from our part-time jobs
goes to feeding Morpeko...

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.740
We can’t do our part as
Team Rocket members with this going on!

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.680
Why’d that thing
settle down here, anyway?!

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.460
It’s not like I have any idea...

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.640
Better to just catch it
so it listens to us, meow.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.730
No way!

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.020
All that worthless thing does is eat!

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.480
Hold on...

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.400
We never actually caught it, so...

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.270
So?

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.650
It goes back to the wild.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.900
Huh?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.830
Kojiro has headed to the mountains
with Morpeko.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.410
How will he return it to the wild?

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.750
Why do I have to...?

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.590
Oh, it’s nothing.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.480
What am I going to do?

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.350
That’s for me? Are you sure?

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.720
It’s actually pretty cute
when it’s not hungry...

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.610
It’s good!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.370
So that’s why they smell so nice.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.760
Keep going, keep going...

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.920
Is it gone?

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.280
Okay!

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.670
I-It’s nothing...
Th-Thank you...

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.520
What should I do...?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.340
Y-You wouldn’t...

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.720
I’ll take everything you’ve got!

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:49.850
Everything?!

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.560
Tasty, aren’t they?
Good to hear it.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.980
You can take your time
and enjoy them.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.530
Stay strong out there...!

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:18.500
Farewell, Morpeko...

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.100
Now we can finally eat in peace!

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.150
Was it a good idea to let Kojiro
handle it on his own though, meow?

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.220
I’m back!

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.750
Oh, good to see you.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.990
You made sure it went back
to the wild, meow?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.200
Of course!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.450
Hah... What a relief. Now...

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.760
Why is <i>that</i> here?!

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.500
I did what you asked...!

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.920
Those are our snacks!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.760
It really followed us...

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.170
It’s asking us “Food?”

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.710
We wouldn’t be out shopping right now
if <i>you</i> hadn’t eaten it all...

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:30.890
How are we getting rid of it?

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.830
Monster Ball, go!

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.540
It’s the brat boys, meow.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.740
Ratta’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.670
All right!
I caught a Ratta!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.480
Great work, Go!

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.220
Ratta! Rat Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.090
A surprisingly violent Pokémon!

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:02.190
With its long fangs, it can gnaw away
even thick concrete with ease!

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.110
Look at how carefree they are,
when we’re suffering so much...

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.680
Oh, I know!

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.130
We can stick them
with Morpeko—

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.320
No, no...
<i>Have them catch</i> Morpeko!

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.110
That’s it!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.820
Nice idea!

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.580
With that decided,
let’s get right to it.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.590
Operation: “Have Them Catch Morpeko”
is a go, meow!

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:31.190
Morpeko, you wait here, meow.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.180
They won’t be able to resist
trying to catch Morpeko.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.890
How about going that way next?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.490
Yeah! Hope we get to see
some new Pokémon!

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:47.480
I’ve already caught most of the Pokémon
around here, so I’m not so sure...

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.130
Why did you come up here?!

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.540
I told you to stay there, meow...

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.760
Just settle down, okay?

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.630
The brat boys are gonna get away...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:11.720
It tastes great!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.270
See?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:22.520
Here, you can eat this.
Just do it quietly.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.690
The brat boys are here, meow!

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.940
You better catch it this time!

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:30.920
Oh, a Pidgeon!

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.210
Huh? Where?

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.170
Over there!

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:34.740
Wait for me!

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.150
Come on...

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.000
I almost had that Pidgeon...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.930
Really stinks.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.290
You there.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.380
Huh, me?

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.380
I see in you a sign that you will meet
your fated Pokémon.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.260
My fated Pokémon?!
Do you mean Mew?!

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.090
I see it!
Your fated Pokémon is...

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.930
My fated Pokémon is...?

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:00.810
There!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:03.890
It’s a Pidgeon!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.170
Umm...

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.650
No! This way, this way!

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.480
Thanks, old lady!

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.110
Wha—?! Old lady?!

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.110
H-Hey, wait, this way,
this way, this way...!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.490
How come the brat boys
never notice it...?

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.190
Please hurry up and catch it, meow...

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.330
They’ve had really bad timing...

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.780
Here’s your delivery
of Pokémon Foods!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.380
Thank you!

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:43.890
Huh? Where’s Morpeko?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.250
Over there, meow.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:47.020
Morpeko!

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:53.180
Stop!

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.750
They don’t need to stop.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.030
This works, meow.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.140
Oh, of course.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.560
Take care of yourself!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.490
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.920
We’re back!

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:54.590
Welcome back, Satoshi, Go.
How’d it go?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.210
I caught a Ratta!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.610
One step closer to Mew, yeah?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.020
But still no luck with Pidgeon.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.970
Just wait until next time!

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.640
I reckon the Pokémon
should be hungry by now.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.140
Oh, right! Satoshi, let’s go!

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:08.980
Yeah!

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:13.420
The new Pokémon Foods came in,
so I left them in the usual place.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.400
Got it!

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.550
Thanks for waiting, guys!

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.530
Time to eat!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.410
I’ll get everything ready now.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.160
A Morpeko?!

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.950
Morpeko! Two-Sided Pokémon!
Electric/Evil type!

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.890
Constantly hungry!

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:48.030
As it eats the seeds stored up in its pocket-like pouches,
it generates electricity!

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:51.930
When hungry, a hormonal change
makes it turn violent!

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:06.490
Don’t worry, Lucario, Aceburn.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:10.000
It must’ve wandered into the box
somewhere along the way.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:39.060
Hey, calm down!

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.210
Okay then...

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:42.990
Neither of them is
giving an inch...

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.890
Yokubarisu, Morpeko,
there’s still plenty more!

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.370
Raichu knew just what to do!

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.190
All right, while it’s distracted...

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.830
Monster Ball, go!

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:37.690
I lost to its appetite...

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.500
Just wait till it calms down,
<i>then</i> you can catch it!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.040
Raichu,
can you take this to Jimeleon?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.480
They might get along
better than I thought!

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.400
Morpeko...
I hope you’re not hungry out there...

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.250
Hey, you listening?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.010
That pest of a Pokémon
is gone now.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:48.010
Time to get back to work!

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:52.950
Our plan for tomorrow is to catch as many Pokémon
as we can here in this shopping mall, meow.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.210
Right.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.030
It really has a big appetite...

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.340
It already ate so much
yesterday...

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.570
Well, a big appetite’s
a good thing!

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:11.990
You can say that again!

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.870
All right, today I’m gonna
catch a Pidgeon!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:16.850
Yeah!

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.720
Where should we go today?

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.190
Good question...

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.220
I lost track of that Pidgeon
around here...

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.240
I hope you find it.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:42.330
Let’s go!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.160
Right!

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.840
Keep it coming!

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.460
We’re in peak form!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.470
What a haul, meow!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.890
What are you doing?!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.260
If you ask us “What are you doing?!”

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.020
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.220
To protect the world from devastation.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:07.190
To preserve world peace.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:10.470
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:13.190
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:14.710
Musashi!

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:15.870
Kojiro!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.470
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:22.620
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.720
Just kidding, meow!

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.860
Team Rocket!

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.430
Give those Pokémon back!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.180
Fat chance!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.990
We’re in peak form today!

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.370
So stay out of our way.

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.730
We’ve eaten well
for the first time in ages!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.180
And we bought lots of
snacks too, meow!

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.880
No chance of them
disappearing meow!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.960
I have no idea what
you’re talking about,

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.820
but you’re not
getting away with this!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.950
Aceburn, go!

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:01.580
Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.210
You asked for it!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.660
Vending, c’mon!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.900
Rocket...

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.280
Vending...

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.080
Secret!

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.850
What’re we gonna get?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.980
The Tiny Bird Pokémon,
Naty!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.980
The Tiny Raccoon Pokémon,
Zigzaguma?!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.860
These are kinda bland.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.000
H-Hey, don’t stare at me...

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.960
Anyway, gonna have to make do!
Zigzaguma! Take Down!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.570
Umm...

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.260
Pull yourself together...

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:54.640
Naty! Peck!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.450
Are you okay, Aceburn?!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:04.930
It’s actually working?

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.770
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.320
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:29.630
Why is...?!

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:30.130
Why is...?

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:31.780
Morpeko?!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.360
I have a bad feeling
about this, meow...

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:41.430
J-Just settle down... okay?

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.530
Aceburn!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:55.410
Pikachu!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.490
That was Stomping Tantrum!

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:00.490
It’s super effective on
both Pikachu and Aceburn, meow!

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.160
Good going,
just keep doing that!

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.630
Why?!

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.920
All that, just for this to happen, meow.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.480
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.270
What was that about?

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.600
No idea...

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.900
Go, look!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.700
Monster Ball, go!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.060
Pidgeon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.140
I did it!

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.830
I caught a Pidgeon!

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:02.160
Great work!

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:10.350
Gah...
What’s wrong with that thing?!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.840
We left behind all the snacks
we bought, meow...

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.690
But...

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.020
Just let it pass by.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.100
Yeah, meow.

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.310
You went looking for us...?

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.220
Morpeko, we’re here!

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:44.220
Hey!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.220
Kojiro, stop, meow!

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:11.790
Let’s stick together,
Morpeko.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.110
You just had to catch it, meow...

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.030
Well, I guess it’s strong?

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:20.480
Let’s see if we can’t
find some use for it.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.050
Now, let’s head back... Huh?

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:34.480
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:39.720
Team Rocket have gained
a new member, Morpeko.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:43.140
Will it someday become
a valuable asset for them?

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:09.630
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:14.580
I am Hodaka,
the leader of Project Mew.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:15.660
Huh?

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:18.910
We’ll have you catch the Alolan Kyukon
that is in the area.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:20.290
Tsurugi...

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.870
You no longer need
to worry about that name.

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:23.780
Kyukon!

00:23:23.780 --> 00:23:25.710
We want to take you back
to where you came from!

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:28.340
So let us catch you!

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:31.030
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:33.980
Let’s Go! Project Mew!!
